 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "현재 수동태 is / are + 과거분사",
   "en": "present passive: is / are + past participle"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "현재 수동태는 행위를 한 사람보다 일 자체가 중요할 때 씁니다. am / is / are + 과거분사 구조이며, 행위자를 말하려면 by를 씁니다 (This book is written by Kim). 재료는 made of / with, 용도는 used for로 말합니다.",
   "en": "Use the present passive when the action matters more than who does it: am / is / are + past participle. Add by to name the doer (This book is written by Kim). Say materials with made of / with and purposes with used for."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "is / are + 과거분사",
     "French is spoken in Switzerland."
    ],
    [
     "복수 / plural",
     "The rooms are cleaned every day."
    ],
    [
     "재료 / material",
     "This cake is made with eggs."
    ],
    [
     "용도 / use",
     "This tool is used for cooking."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "단수 is, 복수 are + 과거분사.",
    "en": "Singular is, plural are + past participle."
   },
   {
    "ko": "행위자는 by + 명사.",
    "en": "The doer is by + noun."
   },
   {
    "ko": "불규칙 과거분사: made, sold, grown, spoken.",
    "en": "Irregular participles: made, sold, grown, spoken."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
